WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.330
MANDEEP WARAICH: My
name is Mandeep Waraich,

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:14.400
and I lead the Industrial AI
Initiative for Google Cloud.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.890
Thank you so much for joining.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.070
Really delighted
to have you here.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:25.020
At Google, we believe that
the goal of every technology

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.250
should be to enrich
our lives, to take

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:34.590
our societies, our
collective humanity, forward.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.910
And do so in a
responsible manner.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.880
So we are constantly thinking
of ways in which technology,

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.830
and particularly AI,
can help us realize

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:50.870
this bright and
promising future.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:55.570
So we've been thinking, how can
we apply our advanced computer

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.510
vision technology
for solving some

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:02.290
of the very hard,
incumbent problems

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:05.319
in the industrial sectors.

00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:10.150
And how can we make these
sectors more efficient and more

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.390
sustainable?

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:16.940
So in the next 50 minutes,
we'll be talking about how,

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:20.310
with industrial
inspection AI, that

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:23.880
is powered by the AutoML
Vision technology,

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:28.300
can help make industrial
inspections more easier,

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:34.500
faster, accurate, and more
importantly, more safer.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.980
And we'll also look at how
two leading companies are

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.610
applying this technology to
the energy and manufacturing

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.355
sector.

00:01:43.355 --> 00:01:44.230
So let's get started.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.390
AI holds great
promise for solving

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:54.500
some real-world problems.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:58.490
From detecting glaucoma
with retinal images,

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:02.060
to processing millions or
even billions of documents

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:07.010
to understand their content,
to automatically moderating

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:10.280
unsafe and
inappropriate content,

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:15.270
we are applying this technology
across all of these use cases.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:19.250
But we also recognize
that developing

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:23.300
this technology, building
these custom vision models,

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.470
is laborious.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:27.380
And it's hard.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:31.970
So we wanted to enable
even the non-programmers

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:35.630
to be able to tap
into the power of AI.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:41.640
And that is precisely why
we created AutoML Vision.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.330
While our standard APIs
are a great powerhouse

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:51.740
for pre-trained models on the
massive Google image datasets,

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:54.950
AutoML allows you to
train custom models that

00:02:54.950 --> 00:03:00.180
are specific to your industry
needs, to your use case needs.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:00.930
How do we do that?

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.710
In a very simple,
clean UI, you are

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:11.970
able to upload the images,
labeled images, if you're

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.850
looking to classify a problem.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:18.660
Or, you can draw bounding
boxes, as we will take a look,

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:23.180
to detect specific objects
within those images.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:26.520
Once you've done that,
with a click of a button,

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.920
you've got a model trained.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.400
And that model can be used
to detect shark species

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.730
in this case, or you
can use that to detect

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:41.905
defects, anomalies, breakage,
in your specific industrial

00:03:41.905 --> 00:03:42.405
products.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:52.600
We're already seeing use cases
with wind turbine degradation

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:57.280
inspection, with outages
on solar panel farms,

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.920
or failures on electric poles.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.260
And we'll be looking into
some of these examples in more

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.415
detail shortly.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.660
At this point, I
want to take a moment

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:12.770
to talk about data
protection and privacy.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:18.180
So your datasets, your
images, are your images.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:20.450
All of these custom
trained models

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:24.230
are used only on your
use cases by you.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.480
Google does not
pull these images

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:30.530
into any common repositories
or use this across customers.

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.795
So your datasets, your images.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.830
We'll take a look at
how this technology can

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:45.060
be applied for aerial
inspection in wind turbines.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:48.810
And then an application of
that on the production line

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.790
in a manufacturing company.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.720
But before I begin there, we
want to share Google's stance

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:58.050
on the use of this technology.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:01.380
Google cares deeply
that its technology

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:05.530
is used for creating a
positive impact in the world.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:10.290
And in that vein, Google
created AI Principles last June.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.470
They set the standard of
the application of these AI

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:14.940
technologies.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:21.090
And we abide by these principles
for any work that involves AI.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:23.610
And similarly, for the
use of this technology

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:28.150
and for this product, we
expect that this technology

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:31.420
be applied in accordance
to the AI principle which

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:34.330
prohibit explicitly the
use of this technology

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:35.485
for any nefarious purposes.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:42.560
So we'll now take a look at
how one of the leading energy

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:46.550
companies in the world is
applying this technology

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:51.650
to create a brighter and
greener future for us all.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.473
Let's take a look at AES
Wind Turbine Inspection.

00:05:54.473 --> 00:05:55.140
[VIDEO PLAYBACK]

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:57.180
- If not the biggest
challenge of our times.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:59.180
Now, we really do
have the technology

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:04.010
to address the issue of carbon
footprint greenhouse gases

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:06.890
from the electric sector.

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:09.080
The AES Corporation
is one of the leaders

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:12.140
in new technologies for
renewables and energy storage.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.060
It's a Fortune 500 company.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:17.600
Our mission is accelerating
a safer and greener energy

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.400
future.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:22.520
- Right now, we have
eight wind farms.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:25.400
Each farm has
different capacity,

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:30.210
starting from 50 turbines,
up to 300 turbines.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:32.900
- They cover large spans
of geography and land.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:36.650
They're spread across
hilltops and mountainsides.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:40.490
- All these turbines
needs annual inspections.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:45.350
Originally, it could take up to
two weeks to do one inspection.

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:49.800
We partnered with leading
drone service company Measure.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.670
Right now, with drones,
we can do it in two days.

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:56.350
And this is safe and quick.

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:58.910
- For a wind turbine inspection,
we go out with our pilots.

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:01.760
And what we're looking for
is cracks or defects, things

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:03.230
that may need to be repaired.

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:06.930
- On a typical inspection, we're
coming back with 30,000 images.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:08.880
Spending four weeks
reviewing images--

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:10.422
I don't think anyone's
going to argue

00:07:10.422 --> 00:07:13.023
that that's the best use of a
highly trained engineer's time.

00:07:13.023 --> 00:07:14.690
- How do we speed
that up and how do you

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:16.340
make it 10x more efficient?

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:18.740
That's where machine
learning and AI comes in.

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:21.170
- We've built a great
end-to-end solution using Google

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:22.660
Cloud's tools and platform.

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:24.680
With the AutoML
Vision tool, we've

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:27.050
trained it to detect damage.

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.120
We're able to eliminate
approximately half

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.920
of the images from
needing human review.

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:33.440
The remaining 50% of
their time can now

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:36.138
be very focused on
identifying that damage

00:07:36.138 --> 00:07:38.180
and really determining
the right course of action

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.740
to remediate it.

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:42.950
Moving from reviewing images
to training machine learning

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:45.500
models-- it's a much higher
order employment opportunity

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:48.450
for people, and one where we're
trying to develop our team.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:50.900
Google Cloud has
been a great partner.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.550
Their technology is consistently
among the world leaders.

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:56.870
And just a great partner to
work with, person to person.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.840
At the end of the day, we won't
reach the cleaner energy future

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:02.900
without advanced tools,
like machine learning.

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:04.700
- Technology will
allow renewable energy

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:06.740
to be cheaper than
conventional energy.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:09.303
Artificial intelligence,
robotics-- this

00:08:09.303 --> 00:08:10.970
is really where the
future is all about.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:17.617
