00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:35.370
The power industry is enormous.

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:37.490
It touches all of our
lives, and the impacts

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.539
are felt around the world.

00:08:39.539 --> 00:08:41.330
The industry
investments are often

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.539
quoted in the
trillions of dollars.

00:08:43.539 --> 00:08:45.320
The opportunities
for improvement

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:48.500
are often in the billions,
if not tens or even

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.797
hundreds of billions of dollars.

00:08:50.797 --> 00:08:52.880
The industry is also going
through significant and

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.560
profound change.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:58.490
Renewable energy is continuing
to fall dramatically in price.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:01.820
Solar, wind, and
battery energy storage

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:05.360
are not just possible,
but practical.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:07.670
The consumer is
also driving change.

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:10.850
They are much more aware
of both the opportunities

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:13.810
and the costs associated
with their energy use.

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:17.490
And the third megatrend
are the new digital tools--

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:21.170
Cloud, AI, and many
others that are changing

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:23.990
the economics of insight.

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:27.230
I'm here today to share one
story, where we've partnered

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:30.260
with Google to improve
lives by accelerating

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:33.000
a safer, cleaner energy future.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.975
We call this, our vision, our
aerial intelligence platform.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:41.760
First, a little bit about myself
and the company I work for.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:42.910
I'm Nick Osborne.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:46.080
I'm the business leader focused
on understanding and applying

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.750
advanced analytic tools,
like artificial intelligence

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:52.230
and machine learning, to
applied business cases.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:53.580
Job's really quite simple.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.890
I accelerate, coordinate,
and facilitate

00:09:55.890 --> 00:10:00.850
the adoption of these new
tools across the organization.

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:02.930
AES is a global power company.

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:06.450
We're headquartered
in the United States,

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:09.360
but operate in 15
countries around the world.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.460
We've made a very
significant commitment

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:17.010
to reduce our carbon intensity
by 70% by the year 2030.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.990
To help us achieve
this, we've made

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:20.580
some very significant
investments

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.260
in new technologies.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.750
We're the world leader
in battery energy storage

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:26.850
using lithium ion batteries.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:30.390
And we're also the largest owner
of solar assets in the United

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:31.950
States.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:34.500
On a personal note, it
feels good to come home

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.030
at the end of the
day and know I'm

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.430
working with a company that's
putting its money where

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:40.650
its mouth is, to
drive that change that

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:41.730
is core to our mission.

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:47.210
Applying new
technologies is core

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.100
to how we operate our business.

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:52.430
Our drone program is
considered world leading

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:54.500
in the energy industry.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:57.340
We developed this program
by partnering with Measure,

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:00.810
Measure is a professional
drone services organization,

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:02.900
and the Measure ground
control software

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:06.650
is an enterprise caliber
drone operations platform.

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:09.770
Through this partnership, we've
improved the cost, safety,

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:12.980
and performance of
our inspections.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:14.990
Another consideration
is that, while we often

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:17.120
hear about the
threat of technology

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:20.930
taking jobs or eliminating jobs,
that's clearly not the case

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:23.000
with what we're seeing
in our drone program

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:25.950
and many other technologies
that we're exploring.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.550
We now have over
170 pilots trained

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:31.430
in our organization, performing
operations in over 100

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:33.352
locations around the world.

00:11:33.352 --> 00:11:35.060
These are employees
with tremendous value

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:37.760
for our company, for their
personal advancement,

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.940
and their broader career growth.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:43.850
Prior to drones,
these inspections

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:45.570
were typically done manually.

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:47.930
So it was either someone
climbing up the turbine

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:50.450
and then rappelling down
to inspect the blade,

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:53.720
or hiking around the turbine
with a large telephoto lens,

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:55.790
trying to capture an
angle and trying to see

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:58.250
if they could detect damage.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:01.490
Neither of these were as
effective, or as efficient,

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:05.160
or as safe, as what we're
able to do with drones.

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:09.050
So using drones, we're now able
to take that partial inspection

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:11.780
that was taking two weeks' of
time and do a full inspection

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:13.280
in two days.

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:15.590
Much lower cost,
much higher quality,

00:12:15.590 --> 00:12:17.450
in a much safer manner.

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:19.700
Tremendous improvement in
efficiency and velocity

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:21.320
in our organization.

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:24.060
But there was one new workflow.

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:26.320
Now, when we do a single
turbine inspection--

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:29.007
a single turbine has
around 300 images.

00:12:29.007 --> 00:12:30.590
When we do an entire
field, this means

00:12:30.590 --> 00:12:35.100
we're coming back with
30,000 or even 60,000 images.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:39.390
This takes a lot of
meticulous and detailed review

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:42.800
to complete the inspection work.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.420
So we saw this as
a great opportunity

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:46.333
for artificial intelligence.

00:12:46.333 --> 00:12:48.500
And this is really where
our partnership with Google

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:51.360
started to grow.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.280
To understand our
journey towards AI,

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:55.450
you need to understand
where we started.

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:57.570
We started with an
investment in talent.

00:12:57.570 --> 00:12:59.880
We sent two classes
of six people

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.340
to Google's Advanced
Solution Lab

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:06.420
for intense training in
supervised machine learning.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:10.640
This cohort became the
foundation for our work in AI.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:12.810
Internally, we referred
to this decision

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.220
as an no regrets decision.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:17.010
Meaning that we were able to
quickly move forward, make

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:21.750
this investment, with little
or no hesitation on our part.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:26.520
A few keys for ROI, is one
is, don't just send IT people

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:28.020
to this training.

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:31.140
A lot of the value from
data science in general

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:34.260
and this program comes from the
mixture of expertise and ideas

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:37.560
that you get when you send
multiple types of people

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:39.340
to the program.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:40.690
The second piece of advice--

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:43.500
and this is maybe a bit
selfish on my part--

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.750
is make sure you have
a good commitment

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:48.840
to work on your projects
after this training.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:51.840
We only sent high performing
individuals to the training.

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:54.060
And the risk with sending
high performing individuals

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.560
is that they're
going to get quickly

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:57.090
pulled back into their day job.

00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:59.340
And that's definitely something
we had to work through

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:01.200
as an organization.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:04.140
So this investment
set the groundwork

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:07.140
to accelerate our progress that
we were making as a company,

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:10.410
and is another example of where
new technologies are increasing

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:14.340
opportunities for our employees.

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:16.570
From this foundation,
we got to work.

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:19.740
We went through a proof
pilot production process,

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:22.830
with each step being a stage
gate for further investment.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:26.370
So starting with our proof,
we built a custom TensorFlow

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:30.450
model, leveraging the openly
available inception V3 vision

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:31.170
model.

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:32.140
And it worked.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:35.580
We were able to detect
damage, but it also showed us

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.650
where our shortcomings were.

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:39.450
Our data needed work.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:41.160
And setting up the
end-to-end platform

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:42.535
was going to be
difficult. And we

00:14:42.535 --> 00:14:44.910
were going to need some help.

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:49.140
So in speaking with Google about
our progress and our learnings,

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:53.470
we discussed the possibility
of partnering on a pilot phase.

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:59.790
So in the pilot phase, we
were using Google's data

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.820
labeling service and
Google's AutoML Vision tool

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:06.190
to really accelerate our efforts
and boost our efficiency.

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:08.400
And again, it worked.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.610
False negatives were
seen as a key business

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:13.360
risk for organization.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:15.000
So not detecting
damage is something

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.310
that we weren't willing to
accept in our inspection

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:18.480
process.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:21.675
So using our most restrictive
precision recall metrics,

00:15:21.675 --> 00:15:23.550
during this pilot phase,
we were able to show

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:25.830
that we could eliminate
30% of the images

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:28.180
from needing any human review.

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:32.910
So that four week review process
was now down to three weeks.

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:36.390
Really accelerate our velocity
and our time to action.

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:39.000
Time to action has really
become one of those key metrics

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.890
that we look at
with this project.

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:46.320
So this gave us the
commitment and ability

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:49.800
to move forward with our
production environment.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:53.220
So our production environment
is a scalable platform for us

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.770
to label images,
train new models,

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:58.110
and manage those
models and production.

00:15:58.110 --> 00:16:00.690
We're still iterating and
refining on this model,

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:03.960
but we're, again, showing
some very promising results.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:07.170
We're now showing that we can
eliminate 50% of the images

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:09.120
from needing any human review.

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:11.160
And the remaining
50% of the images

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:14.220
are now categorized and
classified by type of damage,

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:16.440
further improving
our time to action

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:19.380
and focusing our engineers on
the most important and most

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:20.610
critical types of damage.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.350
Going back to data,
one of the things

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:29.980
that we had learned about
early on was that our data,

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:31.780
we had a lot of
data that was not

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:33.910
the quality or level
of consistency we

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:36.110
needed for machine learning.

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:39.190
So working with Measure, we
developed in nine category

00:16:39.190 --> 00:16:41.170
classification of damage.

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:44.410
This includes things like
cracks, gel coat damage,

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:46.900
different types of
de-lamination and splitting,

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.880
as well as some
non-damage categories,

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:52.030
like serial numbers, lightning
protection points, stickers,

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.810
and whatnot.

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:57.370
So we also worked with Google's
data labeling team to iterate

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:01.240
and walk through many, many
edge cases of different types

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:02.900
of damage that are out there.

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:05.050
We started with a
series of batches, small

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:07.390
in size, doing a full
and complete review

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:09.369
of all the labels
that were coming back.

00:17:09.369 --> 00:17:11.680
But as the quality
of labeling improved

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:13.240
and our batch sizes
improved, we've

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:14.740
moved towards a sample basis.

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:20.095
We also needed to
develop a platform

00:17:20.095 --> 00:17:22.470
to manage the labeling effort,
model training, prediction

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:23.730
process.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.910
Working with Google, we
identified Clear Object

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:30.330
to be our local GCP partner
to help us architect

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:33.360
and develop our platform using
the latest thinking in cloud

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.820
and serverless tools
available from Google.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:38.220
Clear Object has
been a great partner

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:41.280
and worked to quickly
develop this platform for us.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:46.020
The platform leverages AutoML
for our core modeling engine,

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:48.990
Cloud Storage and Cloud SQL
for our image repository

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:53.280
and metadata, as well as
Cloud Functions and App Engine

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:58.100
to manage our interactions
and orchestrations.

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:00.020
Now that we have
this platform, we're

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:02.390
continuing to
improve on the model.

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:05.270
But we're also looking
to expand its use.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:07.460
We're looking at
new business cases--

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:10.190
solar, transmission
infrastructure, and even

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.600
safety--

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:14.540
as well as looking at new
inspection modalities.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:17.720
For example, infrared
and even lidar.

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:20.670
We're also looking at pushing
the model to the edge,

00:18:20.670 --> 00:18:22.173
or in this case, the drone.

00:18:22.173 --> 00:18:23.840
So I'm really excited
to hear about what

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:27.510
LG is going to be sharing next.

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:29.750
Energy is a trillion
dollar business.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:33.760
It impacts lives every day, in
every country around the world.

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:37.360
The challenge and the real
world impact are huge.

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:40.470
If you're interested in
working with or for a company

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:42.960
that is improving
lives by accelerating

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:47.040
a safer, cleaner energy
future, please come talk to me.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.948
Mandeep.

00:18:48.948 --> 00:18:51.378
[APPLAUSE]

00:18:56.028 --> 00:18:57.820
MANDEEP WARAICH: Thank
you very much, Nick,

00:18:57.820 --> 00:19:00.110
for that great presentation.

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:05.770
So we saw how AutoML Vision can
be used for visual inspections

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:11.710
to make them more easy,
faster, accurate, and safer.

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:14.703
In speaking with lot of
experts from the industry,

00:19:14.703 --> 00:19:16.870
we learned that there are
some specific requirements

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:19.360
for manufacturing use case.

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:23.940
A lot of the time, this
data sits on premise.

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:26.560
There are latency requirements.

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:29.290
And most of the
image and datasets

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:32.530
are in a format that requires
it to be processed on the Edge

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:35.800
devices, this be a
mobile phone, this

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:38.665
be an Edge TPU, a CPU or a GPU.

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:45.550
With our AutoML Vision
on Edge solution,

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:48.850
you're able to take your
custom trained model

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:52.360
and then download them
in an Edge device.

00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:56.470
And you can run those inferences
from your Edge devices.

00:19:56.470 --> 00:19:59.440
I think you'd much
rather see that in action

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:02.110
and hear directly from a
manufacturing company which

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:05.300
has deployed these models
on the production line.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:07.180
So it's a great pleasure
for me to invite

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:10.270
Mr. Sungwook Lee from
LG and share more

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:11.440
about this initiative.

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:13.680
Mr. Lee.

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:17.850
[APPLAUSE]

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:19.610
SUNGWOOK LEE: Good
afternoon, everyone.

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:27.340
Thank you for your attention
to our previous presentation.

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:30.750
My name is Sungwook Lee,
and I'm vice president of AI

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:35.530
and big data business
unit at LG CNS.

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:37.820
It seems there
are many, I sense,

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:41.910
passions in our audience today.

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:44.820
I think that if
you are like me, I

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:47.970
expect that we share
many great hopes to apply

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:51.750
AI to lead world solutions.

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:56.300
I also hope this short review
of our collaboration with Google

00:20:56.300 --> 00:21:00.830
AutoML will help you
all in your AI work.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:05.180
Today, we'll be looking at
how LG CNS and Google has

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:10.070
successfully collaborated on AI
image recognition technologies.

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:13.130
And how we have been
applying our [INAUDIBLE]

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:17.960
to vision inspection systems
and several manufacturing

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:18.650
solutions.

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:25.880
Let's begin with a little
background of LG CNS.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:28.820
I think you may know
the name of LG group,

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:32.555
but you don't know about
what kinds of companies

00:21:32.555 --> 00:21:34.550
are in the LG group.

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:36.650
So I want to introduce
some companies.

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:38.900
We have LG Electronics,
which produce

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:41.510
television and refrigerator.

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:44.080
And we have LG
Display, which produces

00:21:44.080 --> 00:21:46.710
world leading OLED panel.

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:51.150
And LG Innotek produces camera
model, so I think half of you

00:21:51.150 --> 00:21:55.860
have already the LG Innotex
camera in your cell phone.

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:57.900
Oh, sorry, smartphone.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:22:01.800
And LG Chemical produces
electric battery.

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.630
So now they're the
world leading company

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:04.810
in that [INAUDIBLE] group.

00:22:04.810 --> 00:22:09.000
So you may know that
almost all the LG group

00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:12.920
companies are working in
the manufacturing industry.

00:22:12.920 --> 00:22:18.840
LG CNS supplies the IT solutions
for the LG Group Affiliates

00:22:18.840 --> 00:22:22.200
and other companies in the
working and the manufacturing

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:23.310
industry.

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:28.980
We are constantly working on
how to best apply AI technology

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:33.290
to improve the
manufacturing processes.

00:22:33.290 --> 00:22:36.850
And we all know that it can
be really challenging to use

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:41.780
big data and AI technology
to ensure product quality

00:22:41.780 --> 00:22:44.120
on a larger scale production.

00:22:44.120 --> 00:22:50.470
This is where our discussion of
Google AutoML comes in today.

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:53.530
LG CNS had started
working with Google AutoML

00:22:53.530 --> 00:22:56.300
in the summer of last year.

00:22:56.300 --> 00:22:58.690
We started our
collaboration after seeing

00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:02.650
that Google was achieving
in their imaging recognition

00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:07.440
technology, because we
thought Google AutoML could

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:11.650
help to improve vision
inspection for LG production

00:23:11.650 --> 00:23:13.500
processes.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:16.863
And to our great satisfaction,
our collaboration

00:23:16.863 --> 00:23:17.655
has been a success.

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:26.070
OK, before we worked with
Google AutoML, actually

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:31.850
we had already developed
our own in-house AI system.

00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:35.250
For those of you familiar with
the manufacturing process,

00:23:35.250 --> 00:23:38.750
you will likely recognize
that the picture there left

00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:45.500
of the screen is the typical
visual inspection system that

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:49.010
relies on the human operators.

00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:53.540
While many production lines
can't have a camera and IoT

00:23:53.540 --> 00:23:56.560
sensors and other
detection technologies--

00:24:00.300 --> 00:24:02.880
while many production
lines can use a camera,

00:24:02.880 --> 00:24:08.970
but it is still hard to find
that little defect efficiently.

00:24:08.970 --> 00:24:11.760
Sometimes non-defective
products are often

00:24:11.760 --> 00:24:15.600
misjudged as defective,
because of minor factors

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:20.820
like small dust particles
or low resolution images.

00:24:20.820 --> 00:24:24.420
And it is still more
effective to rely on people

00:24:24.420 --> 00:24:28.090
to complete visual inspections.

00:24:28.090 --> 00:24:31.190
And while people
get better results,

00:24:31.190 --> 00:24:35.230
that monotony of visual
inspection made by workers

00:24:35.230 --> 00:24:39.650
also leads to many
errors as well.

00:24:39.650 --> 00:24:44.690
To solve this problem,
LG CNS made a transition.

00:24:44.690 --> 00:24:48.290
We moved from the traditional
visual inspection--

00:24:48.290 --> 00:24:51.110
the left image
here you can see--

00:24:51.110 --> 00:24:56.570
to the AI inspection
system shown on the right.

00:24:56.570 --> 00:25:00.260
I'm sure many of you are also
working on the inspection

00:25:00.260 --> 00:25:04.790
technology, so you will
be familiar with the trial

00:25:04.790 --> 00:25:09.770
and error method we did
to improve our system

00:25:09.770 --> 00:25:12.760
with artificial intelligence.

00:25:12.760 --> 00:25:18.550
Anyway, with our
in-house system,

00:25:18.550 --> 00:25:21.280
we increased the
accuracy and performance,

00:25:21.280 --> 00:25:25.480
and even improved our
process speed and efficiency.

00:25:25.480 --> 00:25:28.990
It means that we could reduce
our operation costs also.

00:25:34.200 --> 00:25:37.980
With our in-house
AI system, we were

00:25:37.980 --> 00:25:42.030
able to apply to over
30 production lines

00:25:42.030 --> 00:25:43.890
only in LG Group.

00:25:43.890 --> 00:25:45.690
Some of these include--

00:25:45.690 --> 00:25:48.300
the first picture,
as you can see--

00:25:48.300 --> 00:25:51.060
we could improve
the defect detection

00:25:51.060 --> 00:25:54.620
in LCD and OLED dependence.

00:25:54.620 --> 00:25:57.380
And under in the
middle of the picture,

00:25:57.380 --> 00:26:03.120
we could remove impurities
from the optical film.

00:26:03.120 --> 00:26:06.720
And even improving the quality
control for the production,

00:26:06.720 --> 00:26:11.940
so automotive fabrics can
be made with our in-house AI

00:26:11.940 --> 00:26:14.230
system.

00:26:14.230 --> 00:26:19.100
But even with these
improvement, our system

00:26:19.100 --> 00:26:22.790
wasn't working optimally,
because it still

00:26:22.790 --> 00:26:27.010
required a lot of time and
effort to perform well.

00:26:30.600 --> 00:26:36.460
And now I will talk a
little about the downside

00:26:36.460 --> 00:26:39.310
of this system.

00:26:39.310 --> 00:26:42.440
As is often the
case with success,

00:26:42.440 --> 00:26:46.340
we also ran into some obstacles.

00:26:46.340 --> 00:26:51.230
As we expanded the application
of our AI vision inspection

00:26:51.230 --> 00:26:55.730
into other areas, we have
experienced a shortage

00:26:55.730 --> 00:26:58.940
of skilled AI developers.

00:26:58.940 --> 00:27:03.160
It is very hard to hire the good
AI developers for the company.

00:27:03.160 --> 00:27:06.540
They are located in South Korea.

00:27:06.540 --> 00:27:09.350
So it is very hard times.

00:27:09.350 --> 00:27:14.030
When one AI developer
leaves our company,

00:27:14.030 --> 00:27:19.220
the bad impact is so
big to our company.

00:27:19.220 --> 00:27:22.070
And while we designed
the AI model,

00:27:22.070 --> 00:27:24.920
they needed to spend
lots of time and effort

00:27:24.920 --> 00:27:27.690
to achieve high performance.

00:27:27.690 --> 00:27:32.300
Additionally, as we developed
the model using servers located

00:27:32.300 --> 00:27:36.060
at the production site, the
complexity of architecture

00:27:36.060 --> 00:27:40.340
has been increased, so
it is hard to be solved.

00:27:40.340 --> 00:27:46.430
So now we require the process
to centrally design, and test

00:27:46.430 --> 00:27:48.660
with the model to
the [INAUDIBLE],,

00:27:48.660 --> 00:27:51.300
and to centrally
control the performance

00:27:51.300 --> 00:27:57.000
of the deployed model in
one integrated system.

00:27:57.000 --> 00:27:59.670
Collaboration with
Google has been

00:27:59.670 --> 00:28:03.675
critical to find the
solution to these problems.

00:28:10.160 --> 00:28:16.860
The performance of Google
AutoML has been truly exciting,

00:28:16.860 --> 00:28:22.750
even though our AI
experts don't like it.

00:28:22.750 --> 00:28:27.520
One of the key areas we needed
to improve in our AI system

00:28:27.520 --> 00:28:34.060
was our productivity in terms
of the model development time.

00:28:34.060 --> 00:28:37.630
As you can see in the
diagram on the left,

00:28:37.630 --> 00:28:40.930
our top arrow bar
shows that it took

00:28:40.930 --> 00:28:47.390
a roughly seven days to complete
our model before using AutoML.

00:28:47.390 --> 00:28:53.550
But afterwards, we brought
that down to a mere two hours

00:28:53.550 --> 00:28:56.160
with Google AutoML.

00:28:56.160 --> 00:28:58.020
The other area we
needed to improve

00:28:58.020 --> 00:29:02.130
was the accuracy of our system.

00:29:02.130 --> 00:29:04.150
In addition to being faster--

00:29:04.150 --> 00:29:08.310
from the diagram on
the right picture--

00:29:08.310 --> 00:29:12.780
Google AutoML's performance
exceeded that of the AI experts

00:29:12.780 --> 00:29:14.580
many times.

00:29:14.580 --> 00:29:19.080
Our test results showed
an average 6% improvement

00:29:19.080 --> 00:29:22.290
in terms of performance
we can expect when

00:29:22.290 --> 00:29:24.150
using Google AutoML, I think.

00:29:29.440 --> 00:29:34.450
While we have made advances
using Google AutoML

00:29:34.450 --> 00:29:38.600
and integrating that with
our visual inspection,

00:29:38.600 --> 00:29:42.010
we are still facing
several challenges.

00:29:42.010 --> 00:29:48.410
In many cases, we could not
meet our clients' requirement.

00:29:48.410 --> 00:29:53.510
And we found that many of them
comes from low image quality,

00:29:53.510 --> 00:29:57.810
not from the model that
we made with Google.

00:29:57.810 --> 00:30:02.110
So to solve this
problem, we recently

00:30:02.110 --> 00:30:08.980
launched an immediate
pre-processing research team.

00:30:08.980 --> 00:30:13.010
The members of this
team spend more time

00:30:13.010 --> 00:30:19.430
on exploratory data analysis
and pre-processing data,

00:30:19.430 --> 00:30:25.250
and try hard to augment data for
getting better machine learning

00:30:25.250 --> 00:30:26.370
models.

00:30:26.370 --> 00:30:29.530
So they came to
spend a lot of time

00:30:29.530 --> 00:30:35.590
on thinking how to change the
inspection process itself.

00:30:35.590 --> 00:30:42.970
I estimate now our members
could use their time and effort

00:30:42.970 --> 00:30:46.320
for more strategy work.

00:30:46.320 --> 00:30:51.770
Now we are planning to expand
our business into consulting

00:30:51.770 --> 00:30:58.300
services, so we will
provide expertise

00:30:58.300 --> 00:31:01.370
to enhance the overall
inspection processes

00:31:01.370 --> 00:31:04.260
as a one-step solution.

00:31:04.260 --> 00:31:08.640
We are hopeful that we will
see the first manufacturing

00:31:08.640 --> 00:31:13.960
visual inspection area where
humans and AI share areas--

00:31:13.960 --> 00:31:17.368
the responsibility--
very optimally.

00:31:17.368 --> 00:31:17.910
Do you agree?

00:31:21.820 --> 00:31:23.260
OK.

00:31:23.260 --> 00:31:28.420
I would like to announce that we
have built integrated AI vision

00:31:28.420 --> 00:31:30.770
inspection architecture.

00:31:30.770 --> 00:31:37.930
So our system and Google
AutoML is connected seamlessly.

00:31:37.930 --> 00:31:40.540
With this architecture
we will be

00:31:40.540 --> 00:31:45.970
able to maximize humans'
capability and utilization

00:31:45.970 --> 00:31:48.460
of Google AutoML.

00:31:48.460 --> 00:31:51.430
This architecture starts
from the data science

00:31:51.430 --> 00:31:54.130
parts-- the bottom.

00:31:54.130 --> 00:31:57.260
They will ensure image quality.

00:31:57.260 --> 00:32:00.880
So they will produce
clear imaging

00:32:00.880 --> 00:32:03.490
and will send to
the Google AutoML.

00:32:03.490 --> 00:32:06.730
And Google AutoML
takes the clear imaging

00:32:06.730 --> 00:32:09.850
and produces an AI
model with efficiency

00:32:09.850 --> 00:32:11.550
and with effectiveness also.

00:32:14.850 --> 00:32:21.110
The models-- we completely
manage it with all the history

00:32:21.110 --> 00:32:25.930
data, and performance
status, and automatedly

00:32:25.930 --> 00:32:27.710
learning processes.

00:32:30.302 --> 00:32:35.370
With this architecture,
the LG Group

00:32:35.370 --> 00:32:40.140
now can develop and manage
thousands of AI models

00:32:40.140 --> 00:32:42.150
simultaneously.

00:32:42.150 --> 00:32:44.520
In addition to
vision inspection,

00:32:44.520 --> 00:32:47.640
our goal is to expand
the architecture

00:32:47.640 --> 00:32:50.430
to the other
manufacturing use cases,

00:32:50.430 --> 00:32:52.500
to manage the whole factory--

00:32:52.500 --> 00:32:57.510
equipment, facilities, and
safe things, and so on.

00:32:57.510 --> 00:33:00.610
I think you may think
of many use cases

00:33:00.610 --> 00:33:03.600
we can expand this
integrated architecture

00:33:03.600 --> 00:33:04.920
in the manufacturing industry.

00:33:10.030 --> 00:33:13.730
To this point, we
have gone over how

00:33:13.730 --> 00:33:17.390
collaboration with Google
AutoML has improved

00:33:17.390 --> 00:33:21.640
our visual inspection systems.

00:33:21.640 --> 00:33:26.250
Now let's look to the future.

00:33:26.250 --> 00:33:31.590
Based on our AI integration
success within the LG Group,

00:33:31.590 --> 00:33:33.840
we will keep going
to be positioned

00:33:33.840 --> 00:33:38.260
as leading AI visual inspection
total service provider.

00:33:38.260 --> 00:33:42.340
So we will cover from
the pre-processing area,

00:33:42.340 --> 00:33:45.480
and we will cover
learning the model,

00:33:45.480 --> 00:33:51.452
and then we will manage it all
[INAUDIBLE] with Google AutoML.

00:33:54.350 --> 00:33:57.800
Whether the cause of
poor inspection quality

00:33:57.800 --> 00:34:02.920
is machine-learning equipment,
or the image quality,

00:34:02.920 --> 00:34:07.660
or data labeling, or the
operators themselves,

00:34:07.660 --> 00:34:09.790
working with Google
AutoML, we will

00:34:09.790 --> 00:34:17.679
strive to achieve our goal of
99.9% accuracy and a leak rate

00:34:17.679 --> 00:34:24.510
of 0.001% under all conditions.

00:34:24.510 --> 00:34:30.820
If you were experiencing
similar issues in your industry,

00:34:30.820 --> 00:34:34.929
I hope that this session
could be helpful.

00:34:34.929 --> 00:34:36.590
I really appreciate
your attention,

00:34:36.590 --> 00:34:37.989
and thank you for listening.

00:34:37.989 --> 00:34:38.594
Thank you.

00:34:38.594 --> 00:34:41.842
